    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Hiccups",
            "zh": "打嗝"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " are the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "strange",
            "ref": "v-strange"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " little sounds that come from your mouth. Once or twice is funny, but more than that is "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "annoying",
            "ref": "v-annoying"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Hiccups start much lower in your body—in the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "diaphragm",
            "zh": "横膈膜"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". It’s a "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "muscle",
            "ref": "v-muscle"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " between your "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "lungs",
            "ref": "v-lung"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "stomach",
            "ref": "v-stomach"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". When you breathe in air, it pulls down the air into your lungs. When you breathe out, it lets the air "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "pass through",
            "zh": "穿过"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " your mouth and nose."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Your diaphragm works hard day and night. If you eat too quickly or drink too many soft drinks, your diaphragm may "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "spasm",
            "zh": "痉挛"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". The spasm "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "causes",
            "ref": "v-cause"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " you to draw air into your "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "throat",
            "ref": "v-throat"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", and makes your "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "vocal cords",
            "zh": "声带"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " close. And that causes the “hic” sound."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The hiccups usually go away "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "on their own",
            "zh": "自行"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". But if they go on for hours or days, go to see a doctor. Good luck!"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
